From 7b640f6a0288e8280bc463e682d2cdbc4df8aea6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Jeong, Heon" <blmarket@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 17:30:00 -0700
Subject: Fix memory leak when losing detached client

exit_session and exit_message should be freed when losing a client.
server_client_check_exit is the only place that frees them, and it
returns at once if CLIENT_DEAD is set; server_client_lost sets
CLIENT_DEAD as its first statement. A client that goes away between
being detached and the next pass through check_exit therefore takes both
strings with it, and nothing can reach them afterwards.

check_exit did not clear the pointers after freeing them, so freeing
them in server_client_lost alone would be a double free on the ordinary
path, where check_exit runs first and sets CLIENT_EXITED. Clear them
there and the free when the client is lost becomes a no-op in that case.

exit_session is the name of the session being left, which the user
chooses the length of.

Applies on top of 0005, which puts free(c->path) in the context of the
first hunk. 3.7b's check_exit takes no force argument, so the second
hunk sits at a different line than upstream.
---
 server-client.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/server-client.c b/server-client.c
index 640b7eb..a3707c9 100644
--- a/server-client.c
+++ b/server-client.c
@@ -477,6 +477,8 @@ server_client_lost(struct client *c)
 	free(c->title);
 	free(c->path);
 	free((void *)c->cwd);
+	free(c->exit_session);
+	free(c->exit_message);
 
 	evtimer_del(&c->repeat_timer);
 	evtimer_del(&c->click_timer);
@@ -1952,7 +1954,9 @@ server_client_check_exit(struct client *c)
 		break;
 	}
 	free(c->exit_session);
+	c->exit_session = NULL;
 	free(c->exit_message);
+	c->exit_message = NULL;
 }
 
 /* Redraw timer callback. */
